  {site:'Sheriff Station 4',headline:'The repair-shop break-in',toast:'County news: someone broke into the old Alvarez repair shop. Mina fears what Theo may be hiding; Theo insists the missing letters are nobody else’s business.',reactions:{Mina:'She worries Theo has been hurt, then gets angry that he will not let her help.',Theo:'He says nothing valuable was taken. The empty space where their father’s letters sat tells another story.',Inez:'She offers Mina a quiet place to talk, without asking for details.',Cal:'He remembers hearing a late-night call about a forced door, but cannot make out who reported it.',Ruth:'She wonders whether the stolen letters belonged with the history of the town.',Ari:'She sketches the repair shop with its dark doorway left unfinished.',Sol:'He checks the unofficial library catalog for any mention of the missing letters.',June:'She asks her father whether the sheriff ever found out who did it.'}},
  {site:'Motel Solstice',headline:'The guest who never checked out',toast:'County news: Room 8’s summer guest, Ellis Vale, vanished before checkout years ago. June wants the old record found; Sol remembers a name missing from the library catalog.',reactions:{Mina:'She thinks of the families who still set a place for someone who is gone.',Theo:'He says people leave town all the time, but keeps turning the motel key over in his hand.',Inez:'She hopes someone looked for Ellis with patience, not just paperwork.',Cal:'He remembers an old radio bulletin about a missing motel guest, though the name escapes him.',Ruth:'She recalls a library book returned from Room 8 long after the guest disappeared.',Ari:'She draws the motel sign with one window lit, though the building was dark.',Sol:'He recognizes Ellis Vale from a name that was quietly removed from the library index.',June:'She wants to know why the county stopped looking, and whether anyone ever told Ellis’s family.'}},
  {site:'Drain 9',headline:'The water running uphill',toast:'County news: people swear the current in Drain 9 runs uphill. Cal heard the same thing on the radio; Ari says the water in her sketch is moving the wrong way.',reactions:{Mina:'She tells Lila not to go near the drain, then admits she has always wondered what is down there.',Theo:'He says a slope can fool your eyes, but volunteers to check the tunnel anyway.',Inez:'She remembers the clinic weather vane pointing against the wind on the same night.',Cal:'He is sure a caller described the uphill current years ago, in a voice he still recognizes.',Ruth:'She finds an old library clipping about water flowing toward the ridge, dated decades apart.',Ari:'She has drawn the current moving uphill without meaning to; now she cannot make it flow the other way.',Sol:'He has found the same impossible observation in three unrelated county records.',June:'She says she will believe it when she sees it, then avoids looking away from the drain.'}}
 ].map(event=>({...event,siteIndex:sites.findIndex(site=>site.name===event.site)}));

