108:  Cal:['Can you speak up just a little? I don’t want to miss what you’ve been finding.','I remember you. You’re the one making a map of places most folks pass by.','It’s good having someone to compare notes with. I trust your eye for a detail.'],
109:  Ruth:['A good walk can make a person notice what they’ve been carrying. What did you notice today?','You’ve been back a few times. I’m beginning to think of you as part of the neighborhood.','I saved you a book recommendation. You seem like someone who lets a story linger.'],
110:  Ari:['I’ve been drawing the places you find. The ones you describe always look a little different in my sketchbook.','You came back! Tell me one thing you saw that you think nobody else noticed.','I put a little mark for you on my county map. You’re part of it now.'],
